// PERSONAL vertical — "brief me for my next meeting."
//
// Orbital pulls your next meeting from a privacy-safe local MOCK (no real Gmail/
// Calendar access) and hands back the brief + attendees (name / email / company).
// Because each attendee's `company` is a uk.gov.CompanyName, the brain backgrounds
// the firms straight from the meeting (query 3) — no integration declared
// anywhere; they compose because they share semantic types.
//
// The mock op takes a CalendarSelector ("next") so Orbital plans a clean targeted
// lookup. Flip personal.taxi's baseUrl to a read-only Google MCP shim to go live.

// 1) The brief — title, start time, location.
given { sel : brain.CalendarSelector = "next" }
find { brain.MeetingBrief }

// 2) The attendees — name / email / company (a bound collection).
// given { sel : brain.CalendarSelector = "next" }
// find { brain.MeetingAttendee[] }

// 3) THE PAYOFF — brief me, the attendees, AND background an attendee's employer
//    with the SAME router. Feed a `company` (a uk.gov.CompanyName) to the company
//    spine: Orbital discovers GLEIF (LEI + Companies House number + registered
//    postcode + status) from the name alone — zero wiring between calendar and
//    the gov-uk APIs. Verified live (Monzo Bank -> LEI 213800PLUYXGZ8LU7T61,
//    company 730427, EC2A 2AG). Add WikidataEntity / weather / crime to taste.
// given {
//   sel  : brain.CalendarSelector = "next"
//   name : uk.gov.CompanyName = "Monzo Bank"
// }
// find {
//   meeting   : brain.MeetingBrief
//   attendees : brain.MeetingAttendee[]
//   employer  : uk.gov.apis.gleif.LeiRecord
// }
